        "B (Claude Opus, final)": "'petition refers_to first_house' was never in dispute. The petition was about the missing Latch from the start (ch1 'a room was missing from the Tin Orchard ... the Latch'). The correction is that Lio is the room's own name, not a signer (ch1 'Lio isn't a person. It's what the missing room calls itself when it wants to be found'; 'the petition had mistaken a room's name for its signer'). A fact like first_house name 'Lio' (or petition signed_by nima, ch1 'I signed the petition that arrived') would carry it."
